<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Italian East Africa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Africa Orientale Italiana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Italian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a> was the colonial federation created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1936 after the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, combining Ethiopia with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Italian Somaliland</a>. It was governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a>. It was the largest territorial creation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> but was lost to British and Allied forces in 1941.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/italian-east-africa.jpg" alt="Italian East Africa" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: F l a n k e r · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Italy_(1861-1946)_crowned.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
